Subject: [PATCH] TEACH-ZALLUP: the Teach page's In / Out Z All Up and the
 Index tab's four Servo buttons (golden uteach) -- they were on the page with
 no handler

motor.access gets two uteach actions (kActions rows, dispatch, bodies at the EOF of WebMotorAccess.cpp):
  teachZAllUp      golden btnInZAllUpClick :4466 / btnOutZAllUpClick :4480 -- every Z of that arm (InArmZIndex /
                   OutArmZIndex over In/OutArmSuck.iMotRow x iMotCol, the backend's GoldenTeachFixedMotors) gets the
                   single home Teach's / Motor Test's HOME already starts (DoHome: 1203 DS402 home + case 500 ZSafePos,
                   non-1203 golden ProcessSingleMotorHome); Enable=0 rows -> golden case 200 HomeFlag=1, nothing sent;
                   no CheckCanMove / IsCanQuickJogMove (golden has none); a home already running is not re-issued;
                   ack caption Homeing... (golden DoZHome).
  teachIndexServo  golden btnZ1ServoClick :4253 / btnZ2ServoClick :4270 / btnArm1YServoClick :2919 (btnArm2YServo
                   shares the handler) -- golden's fixed motor (MTestZ1 / MTestZ2 / MTestY1 [+MTestY2 on a 4-axis
                   Index]), target = actual servo state inverted, else golden's static; a 1203 row goes through
                   DoServo (Enable=0 refusal, brake hold, SvOn), another row is refused (golden Gali_Command has no
                   path here); fAllMotorHome=false.
SystemStart and an open hand teach refuse both (dispatcher). Live backend: GoldenTeachFixedMotors ->
W906_TeachFixedMotorsLive (EOF). ctest WebMotorAccess: section [ZALLUP] (+38 checks) and the catalog section
now expects the web JSON with the six new uteach rows (57 commands, 41 actions, live 36) -- deploy
web/JSON/motor-access.json (+ JSON/js/motor-access.js) with this commit.

